Apple has been phasing out the SIM card tray on iPhones, with the latest models relying solely on eSIM technology in select countries.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iPhone-18-Pro-Burgundy-1-1.jpg" alt="" width="1351" height="760" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063606" /><br/>
According to Apple, the iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max support eSIMs only in these countries and regions:<br/>
<br/>
<ul><br/>
  <li>Bahrain</li><br/>
  <li>Canada</li><br/>
  <li>Guam</li><br/>
  <li>Japan</li><br/>
  <li>Kuwait</li><br/>
  <li>Mexico</li><br/>
  <li>Oman</li><br/>
  <li>Qatar</li><br/>
  <li>Saudi Arabia</li><br/>
  <li>United Arab Emirates</li><br/>
  <li>United States</li><br/>
  <li>U.S. Virgin Islands</li><br/>
</ul>iPhone 17 Pro models are eSIM-only in the same countries, so there is no change this year.<br/>
<br/>
iPhone 18 Pro models continue to have a tray for a physical SIM card in all other countries around the world, including in the U.K. and the rest of Europe.<br/>
<br/>
If you are unaware, an eSIM is essentially a digital version of a SIM card.<br/>
<br/>
Apple says eSIM-only iPhone models are equipped with a larger battery that fills the space formerly occupied by the physical SIM card tray. Earlier today, we reported on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/iphone-18-pro-max-battery-capacities/">iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max battery capacities</a> listed on EU regulatory labels, but note that these figures are for models that still have a SIM card tray.<br/>
<br/>
Apple started phasing out SIM cards starting with the iPhone 14 series, in the U.S. only at first.<br/>
<br/>
iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max models sold in European countries, Australia, New Zealand, Singapore, South Korea, and elsewhere still have nano-SIM card trays alongside eSIM support. In China, the devices support one of the following combinations: two nano-SIM cards, one nano-SIM card and one eSIM, or two eSIMs. <br/>
<br/>
iPhone Duo features an eSIM-only design worldwide.<br/>
<br/>
